WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.800
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 8:
Tools, Machines, and Everyday Items.

2
00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:12.180
This unit is all about the tools, machines, and
everyday items we use at home, at school, and at work.

3
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:18.980
You will learn the names of many useful objects — from a
stapler and a microwave to a telescope and a helicopter.

4
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:25.040
You will also learn how to describe what these things
do, how to give safe instructions for using them,

5
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.600
and how to talk about working together as a crew.

6
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:35.040
By the end of the unit, you will be ready to read
and enjoy this unit's mystery story, “The Attic Clue”,

7
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:41.440
about a class in Rwanda who discover old tools in
a dusty attic and build something amazing together.

8
00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:46.980
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:54.300
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name and
describe many tools, machines, and everyday items in English.

10
00:00:54.300 --> 00:01:00.680
You will also describe an object using adjectives
and a relative clause with who, that, or which.

11
00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:05.220
You will also say what people have to do
to stay safe when using tools and machines.

12
00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:08.140
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:16.460
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: invention,
description, protection, attention, national, according.

14
00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:22.120
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:26.080
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:31.880
The reading sequence includes The Right
Tool for the Job and A Look at the Stars.

17
00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:33.680
Read actively.

18
00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:38.700
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:42.520
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:48.680
The first language focus is Defining
Relative Clauses (who, that, which).

21
00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:55.620
A defining relative clause is an extra part of a sentence
that tells us exactly which person or thing we mean.

22
00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:02.980
For example, in “the tool that joins papers,” the
words “that joins papers” tell us it is a stapler.

23
00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:07.080
This helps us describe the tools
and machines in this unit clearly.

24
00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:13.680
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:19.620
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Describe an Everyday Item.

26
00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:24.040
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.300
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.900
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.240
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:38.280
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:40.960
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:47.820
Use the AI tutor for hints and feedback any time, and
bring your questions to a live session too if you join one.
